      "comment": "MCVEIGH (2) is a very progressive 4YO gelding from the powerful Adam Trinder stable who looks set for his best season yet after an impressive all-the-way win here nearly 3 weeks ago. He skips a grade for this, and drops half a kilo. Hard to beat again, especially from the pole position. SOUTHERN AURORAS (4) has been holding her form nicely since progressing to this grade in early August. She would prefer some cut in the ground, and with conditions to suit, she will be right in the finish here. BERSERKER (5) is a consistent gelding, who does not win often. He resumes from a spell with a couple of strong trial efforts under his belt, and is nicely weighted for this assignment. Check for any market moves. THE TRINE (1) is a lightly tried gelding with plenty of talent fresh up from a spell. He has trialled up, cops a decent gate, and will be ready to rumble. Keep safe. PLATINUM REGGAE (6) has needed both of her starts this prep and should now be ready to show some worthwhile form.",
